This is not obvious but it is true - Save scumming prevents
ascension.  What happens is you tend to get in progressively
worse situations and use save scumming to get yourself out
of the tactical part of the situation without learning anything
about the strategic part of the situation.

My latest - I lost my best Samurai ever to Famine on the Astral
plane.  I didn't make it to the first altar to see if it was the right
one.  I tried blasting forward and avoiding combat with any
monster behind me, not a tactic to use with any of the Riders.
I'm pretty sure I should have been generating monsters that
push the stronger ones away from me rather than fighting my
way through the crowd.  Taming or similar ...  Good weapons
and high AC doesn't cut it on Astral.  I also should have switched
to Sunsword to be able to see ahead so I could jump into open
spaces instead of fighting my way through one step as a time.
Having a light source makes all the difference when you're
wearing jumping boots.

But if I'd save scummed would I have managed to learn all of
that from a single failure?  I sure didn't back when I did save
scum.  Yet in the end I didn't ascend save scumming either.


